@frenchoniulator Your reply has nothing to do with the parent post. 

You’ve been spamming your little internet feud on all my posts. 

I don’t even work at X anymore; I don’t know what you want from me.

Menese Protocol is live, in production, and decentralising through the NNS.

The execution layer of chain key, turned into a product.

Chain key lets a canister hold a signing key no node, server or company ever sees in full. We built the rest: native canisters that read the market through HTTP outcalls, decide on chain, sign with threshold keys and submit the transaction on the destination chain. No bridge. No custodian. The first cross chain swap architecture of its kind on ICP.

21 chains, one wallet, one identity.
Bitcoin $BTC, Ethereum $ETH, Arbitrum $ARB, Optimism $OP, Base, Polygon $POL, Monad $MON, Solana $SOL, Sui $SUI, Aptos $APT, NEAR $NEAR, TON $TON, TRON $TRX, Cardano $ADA, XRP $XRP, Litecoin $LTC, CloakCoin $CLOAK, Hyperliquid $HYPE, Bittensor $TAO, Robinhood Chain, and ICP $ICP itself. Real transactions, built and signed by the canister, on every one of them.

Safe execution inside the venues people already use.
@RaydiumProtocol swaps, concentrated liquidity and LP
@pumpdotfun launches
@BackedFi xStocks on Solana
@RobinhoodApp Chain: a Stocks Center with 25 tokenized stocks, bought and sold in USDG, swapped cross chain to USDC
@Uniswap V3 on mainnet and the L2s, v4 on Robinhood Chain
@aave supply and @LidoFinance staking
@circle CCTP for native USDC across Solana and the EVM chains
@THORChain cross chain swaps
@HyperliquidX spot with native take profit and stop loss
@CetusProtocol on Sui, @MinswapDEX on Cardano, @ICPSwap on ICP, @finance_ref on NEAR
Every order is signed inside the canister and broadcast by you. No custody, ever.

Stables, staking and liquidity from the same wallet.

USDC, USDT and DAI on the EVM chains, USDG on Robinhood Chain, RLUSD on XRP, DJED on Cardano, ckUSDC and ckUSDT on ICP. MENES, mSOL, haSUI, TAO and TRX staking. LP on Raydium CLMM, Uniswap V3 and our own CLOAK/USDC and MENES/ICP pools.

The first sovereign automation, inside the venues themselves.

Most of these venues have no automation of their own. 

The canister adds it, and your strategy executes straight into the venue you chose: DCA, take profit, stop loss, trailing stops and LP rebalancing on Raydium and Uniswap V3, spot DCA with native TP/SL on Hyperliquid, DCA and TP/SL on Cetus, Minswap and the XRPL DEX. Price by outcall, decision on chain, threshold signature, real transaction. No bot on somebody's server. Your strategy, your keys, your rules.

Connected, and open to builders.

WalletConnect is built in: pay or sign from your Menese wallet on Ethereum, Base, Optimism, Polygon and Arbitrum, no seed phrase anywhere. The Menese SDK and a permissionless gateway expose the same execution layer: get a key, start free, pay per action. Agent Mode lets an AI agent send, swap and bridge across the same chains without ever holding a key.

A milestone delivered: the DAO is in place.

We promised to decentralise, and the SNS is live on the NNS. When the swap concludes, the canisters pass to the DAO: upgrades, treasury and direction decided by MENES neurons, not by one company. Next: tier one exchange listings, and enterprise expansion through businesses and agents building on the SDK.

The swap sale is open.

10,000,000 MENES, one window on the NNS, open until 13 October. The only allocation sold by the protocol itself, out of a fixed supply of 100,000,000. No inflation, no minting, ever.

https://t.co/6lI9KStq1S

Built quietly, months in production, hundreds of active users holding and moving real funds. That changes today.

$ICP $MENES $HOOD #ICP #DeFi #ChainKey
